OL,3,GNEWSALake District littering 'creating
OL,4,Ano-go areas'
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople feel littering in the Lake
OL,7,FDistrict is worsening, with parts of it
OL,8,Fbecoming a "no-go area for those
OL,9,Fwanting to enjoy its natural beauty", a
OL,10,Fcharity's survey has found.
OL,12,FTwo thirds (68%) of those who responded
OL,13,Fto the Friends of the Lake District's
OL,14,Fonline questionnaire said the situation
OL,15,Fwas becoming worse, with 23% saying it
OL,16,Fwas about the same as 2025.
OL,18,FRespondents highlighted a catalogue of
OL,19,Fproblems, including littering - which
OL,20,F96% had experienced - some form of
OL,21,Fillegal or inconsiderate parking (84%),
OL,22,Fand fly-camping (73%).
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,402,400,260,160,0,100
